(Mira)

12
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:53,560
(Celebrity - Cafeteria Gang)

13
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,280
So, the thing we were going to...

14
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:29,320
So, the thing we were going to...

15
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,960
You see, this particular news

16
00:01:35,039 --> 00:01:37,479
is extremely important.

17
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:40,440
Therefore, its value,

18
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,440
is a little higher.

19
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,759
So...

20
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:17,960
So...

21
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:19,160
Hey!

22
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,160
I don't want to know anymore!

23
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,640
And pay for the cupcake and your drink, too!

24
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,160
Namwan, calm down.

25
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,480
But if I tell you,

26
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,880
don't tell anyone else, okay?

27
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:27,920
Fine.

28
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:32,120
I saw Mr. Chat and Mr. Seungwoo

29
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:35,240
in the car just the two of them alone!

30
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:37,680
Oh my gosh! That's insane!

31
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:41,200
Who rode in the car alone with Mr. Seungwoo?

32
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,520
Oh my gosh! You scared me Ms. Mira!

33
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:46,400
I saw Mr. Chat with Mr. Seungwoo

34
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:48,040
the two of them went out together!

35
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,720
And, more importantly,

36
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:53,280
Mr. Seungwoo opened the door for Mr. Chat.

37
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:55,640
Oh my, if they weren’t at the company,

38
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,520
if it were just the two of them alone,

39
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,400
Mr. Seungwoo would carry Mr. Chat to the car.

40
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,320
How enviable.

41
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,560
If Mr. Seungwoo plays favorites like this,

42
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:12,360
it probably won’t be good for our team, Mira.

43
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,840
My old friend still hasn’t dropped that habit

44
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:19,440
of cozying up to the boss to save his own skin.

45
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:46,079
(Nueng)

46
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:52,440
Yes, Nueng?

47
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,720
Where are you, Chat?

48
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,720
I have a meeting scheduled with a client.

49
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,680
What's the matter?

50
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,480
It's nothing.

51
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,440
It's just, I didn't see you.

52
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,640
So I got worried.

53
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,440
Thank you.

54
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,680
Oh, yes.

55
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:17,680
Why do you have to lie?

56
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,120
So you expect me to tell them that

57
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:25,160
you just dragged me into your car out of nowhere

58
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,960
and took me to who-knows-where?

59
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,760
So can you tell me where we're going yet?

60
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:01,040
Why did you take me here?

61
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,280
You'll find out soon enough.

62
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:13,280
Hello.

63
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:18,440
Hello.

64
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:21,360
This is Mr. Chat.

65
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,360
I received your data.

66
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:27,760
It's only because of Mr. Seungwoo that I came to look at it.

67
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:31,160
So how is my data?

68
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,920
I've reviewed your data,

69
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,640
and I have to admit it's very good.

70
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,400
The data is solid, well researched,

71
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,360
and cites research findings.

72
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:46,280
Let me just check it once more,

73
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,240
and if everything is in order,

74
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,800
I'll issue the certificate for you.

75
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:49,840
Thank you.

76
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,280
How did you manage to book the doctor?

77
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:59,920
Mr. Seungwoo often invites me to be

78
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,920
a consultant at Vega Lab Korea.

79
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:04,720
I've actually co-developed several of

80
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,400
the products on the Korean side.

81
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,600
Actually, we're close.

82
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,560
You've never told me before.

83
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:15,200
Well, you didn't ask.

84
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:18,440
Besides,

85
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,000
if I'd told you, it wouldn't have been a surprise.

86
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,120
Why did you help me today?

87
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:44,240
I only helped get the documents

88
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,120
to the doctor to look at.

89
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,960
Whether it passes or not

90
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,640
depends entirely on your own ability.

91
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:54,720
Thank you.

92
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,480
I thought

93
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,680
you were only good in...

94
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,880
I think we should head back now.

95
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,640
Please get in.

96
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,000
Oh wow.

97
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,240
Why don’t you ask the staff

98
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,159
which ones Mr. Chat hasn’t tried yet?

99
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:46,280
I’m worried you’ll spend ages picking,

100
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,400
and turns out he’s already had them.

101
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,760
What do you mean?

102
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,760
Wait, you don’t know?

103
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,480
Mr. Nueng buys from this shop for Mr. Chat.

104
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,840
Everyone on Team B knows.

105
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,400
Here, let me show you a photo.

106
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,600
Here.

107
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,560
Mr. Nueng.

108
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,240
How come I’ve never seen him before?

109
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,960
Let me see the photo too.

110
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:13,160
Of course you’ve never seen him.

111
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:15,160
Mr. Nueng is a graphic designer on Team A.

112
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,600
Even though he's on different team,

113
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:18,440
Ms. June gossips about it all the time,

114
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:20,720
how he’s been secretly helping Mr. Chat.

115
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:23,360
Dude,

116
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:26,160
Chat might be weak against persistent guys.

117
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,800
“True love loses to whoever stays close.”

118
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,520
I’m the closest, Floyd.

119
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,880
We live together, you know?

120
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,600
We were together for so long,

121
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:37,880
I don’t believe he can let go of me that easily.

122
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,200
Besides,

123
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,799
I’ll make Chat fall in love with me again.

124
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,080
It’s not that easy, kiddo.

125
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,160
What else?

126
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,920
Because there’s more than one person

127
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,000
who likes Mr. Chat.

128
00:08:57,440 --> 00:09:02,840
(Jeno)

129
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,120
Aren't you going to answer their call?

130
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,120
They might have something important to say.

131
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,000
It's probably nothing.

132
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:21,320
If you’d like to talk in private,

133
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,880
I can pull over so you can get out and talk.

134
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,720
It's fine.

135
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:29,640
But your partner...

136
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,000
They're not my partner.

137
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:35,760
(Jeno)

138
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,680
He and I are nothing to each other.

139
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,280
Hey!

140
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,920
What's wrong with it?

141
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:57,640
It's hot?

142
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:58,840
No, that's not it.

143
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,160
Did the battery die?

144
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,880
And I have to submit it by next hour.

145
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:04,760
What's wrong with it?

146
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:09,320
The screen isn't even hot.

147
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,880
Making all that noise isn't going to

148
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:14,080
get the computer to turn on for you.

149
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,280
It's my computer,

150
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,600
I can do whatever I want with it.

151
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,440
What's wrong with it?

152
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,400
Move over.

153
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,800
What's wrong?

154
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,880
Come here.

155
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:38,040
Hey!

156
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,560
Just save your breath to thank me later.

157
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:53,600
Tried giving it a whack? Maybe it’ll work.

158
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:58,800
You’re just like you were back in school.

159
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:01,720
Whenever anything broke, you told me to whack it.

160
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:04,040
Where did you even get that theory from?

161
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,120
Whoa! / Whoa!

162
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,200
Thank me right now.

163
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:11,000
Give it back. I need to work. / Thank me.

164
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,040
Give it to me.

165
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:28,920
I'm sorry.

166
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,880
What's wrong with me?

167
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,800
You like Nueng, right?

168
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:04,800
I saw that.

169
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,960
It was just an accident, right?

170
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,400
Don't tell anyone.

171
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:14,840
Come on, if you like him just tell him.

172
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,040
You think others can't tell?

173
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,880
Just tell him. Why hide it?

174
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:33,520
(Chat, where are you right now?)

175
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:14,880
Mr. Chat.

176
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,840
Yes?

177
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,400
Thank you.

178
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,240
Please send me an update tomorrow.

179
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,800
Of course.

180
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,320
Who dropped you off?

181
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,400
My new boss.

182
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:09,840
Here.

183
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:15,800
The new boss from Korea.

184
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,640
The whole company is buzzing with rumors.

185
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:20,560
He seems especially interested in Mr. Chat too.

186
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:22,720
Especially? How?

187
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:25,120
How could he not be special?

188
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,840
On the first day he arrived,

189
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,880
he called Mr. Chat for a private conversation.

190
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:31,960
This morning, someone saw

191
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:33,960
Mr. Seungwoo dragged Mr. Chat into his car

192
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,800
and went somewhere alone.

193
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:38,200
So? Does that sound special to you?

194
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:45,440
Let me help you.

195
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:46,960
Also

196
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,360
I bought you snacks upstairs.

197
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:04,880
Mira, currently, Team B's project

198
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,160
has been approved!

199
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:10,120
How could Team B’s project get approved?

200
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:13,320
It didn’t just pass,

201
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:15,320
it’s waiting to go into production.

202
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
But yesterday they were

203
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,800
still asking the expert team for information.

204
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:28,120
Team B doesn’t just have the data now.

205
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,800
They’ve actually got the expert

206
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,720
herself on board as a consultant.

207
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,480
Someone at that level isn’t easy to get access to,

208
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,440
so somebody must have helped.

209
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,560
Or maybe it’s because Mr. Seungwoo

210
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:47,360
disappeared with Mr. Chat all day yesterday.

211
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,720
Maybe all night too, I’d guess.

212
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,600
No wonder the work sailed through like that.

213
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:59,640
And here’s our sales summary for this quarter.

214
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,320
We grew 13.6%.

215
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:08,400
Since the company is expanding production,

216
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:12,560
I want to create one more Team B.

217
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,160
I’ve already spoken with your supervisors,

218
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,599
and I’ve chosen Chat

219
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,359
as the new Team B leader.

220
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:23,800
But Mira and I

221
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:26,000
worked on this project together.

222
00:17:26,079 --> 00:17:27,000
My decision is made.

223
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,520
This meeting is adjourned, that’s all.

224
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:34,560
Notify HR.

225
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,120
Yes, Ms. Nichakorn.

226
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,280
I’ll go talk to Ms. Nichakorn for you.

227
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:46,000
Ms. Nichakorn,

228
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:48,080
it’s just that Mira and I, the two of us...

229
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,680
Congratulations.

230
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:50,640
I’m glad to be

231
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:53,440
working with the new Team B leader.

232
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:57,240
Dr. Wannana was right to entrust you to me,

233
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,520
so work hard.

234
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,560
What about Mira?

235
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,320
I’ll think it over again.

236
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,480
What is it this time?

237
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:41,320
The whole company is talking. They say

238
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:43,360
Mr. Seungwoo secretly took the Team B leader

239
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,840
to find important information.

240
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:47,080
I think that’s unfair.

241
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:48,800
And what do you want me to do about it?

242
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:50,880
If this is a competition,

243
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,160
it should be fair to every team.

244
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:56,440
Then go and find evidence,

245
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:58,120
and I’ll deal with it.

246
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,760
Evidence?

247
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:02,480
Evidence that he showed favoritism

248
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,480
or overstepped his authority.

249
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,080
If it’s only a rumor,

250
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:09,440
it’s just office gossip.

251
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:12,360
But if the rumor turns out to be true,

252
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,720
someone will have to take responsibility.

253
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:48,560
You seem a bit off today.

254
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,320
Is something the matter?

255
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:52,600
You see...

256
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:55,720
I heard some staff

257
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:58,000
talking about you and Team B, saying...

258
00:19:58,080 --> 00:19:59,280
They’re saying

259
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:01,360
I look unfair, right?

260
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:05,040
I'm afraid the staff will think badly of you.

261
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:09,680
For me,

262
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:13,480
I only care about the work.

263
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,240
If Team A made a mistake,

264
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:19,160
I’d have to help Team A the same way.

265
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,320
But Mr. Seungwoo, they...

266
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,400
I can’t stop what other people think,

267
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:24,440
but

268
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,400
I know very well

269
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:27,960
what I’m doing myself.

270
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:32,720
Thank you for worrying about me.

271
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:43,960
Yay!

272
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:45,680
Good job!

273
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:58,000
Om my gosh!

274
00:20:58,080 --> 00:21:00,520
I’m so happy

275
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,120
our Team B managed to

276
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:04,120
gather all the information!

277
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:08,040
Right?

278
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:10,760
Yesterday we were working ourselves half to death.

279
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:14,520
It’s because we have such a capable leader

280
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,760
that everything went through.

281
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:19,440
I’m not that capable.

282
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:21,800
If you want to thank someone, thank Mr. Seungwoo

283
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,440
for helping us.

284
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:26,480
Geez, he’s helping this much.

285
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:27,840
Is he after something?

286
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:32,600
He’s just doing his job.

287
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:35,960
But right now people are gossiping like crazy

288
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:38,120
about you and the boss.

289
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,800
Don’t care

290
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,560
what anyone says or thinks.

291
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:45,880
Because right now

292
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:48,640
it’s time to celebrate!

293
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:52,520
Congratulations.

294
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:01,080
Thank you, Mr. Seungwoo.

295
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:04,160
Gamsahamnida!

296
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:06,600
Without you, Mr. Seungwoo,

297
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:09,920
our whole team would have been fired for sure.

298
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,640
You all were already doing good work.

299
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:16,120
I only helped you find what was missing.

300
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:19,600
I hope you’ll do this well

301
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:21,800
on the next stage too.

302
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,080
Yes.

303
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,480
One please.

304
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:30,400
He seems kinder today.

305
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:32,560
Especially handsome, too.

306
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:33,680
So?

307
00:22:33,760 --> 00:22:35,120
Six o'clock.

308
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,960
True, normally... He's here.

309
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:42,040
Mr. Chat.

310
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:43,120
Yes?

311
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,000
please stay

312
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:48,920
for a meeting with me after work.

313
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:51,720
I would like to propose this product

314
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,640
to Vega Lab Korea as well.

315
00:22:58,680 --> 00:22:59,800
Yes, sir.

316
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:11,920
After work!

317
00:23:12,480 --> 00:23:15,360
Is all the information I asked you to find ready?

318
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:17,240
I’ve taken care of it.

319
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:18,520
Okay, good.

320
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:19,960
Now on with the next steps.

321
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,600
Ms. Mira!

322
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:23,640
Ms. Mira!

323
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:24,880
Ms. Mira!

324
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:28,120
What's wrong, Namwan? Calm down.

325
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,040
Just now,

326
00:23:29,120 --> 00:23:30,280
I heard Mr. Seungwoo

327
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:32,600
set up a private meeting with Mr. Chat tonight

328
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,960
after work.

329
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:36,720
I wonder if they’re going to work, or what

330
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:38,080
exactly they’re going to be doing.

331
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:42,880
Ms. Mira!

332
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:44,480
I know.

333
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:51,840
See you tomorrow, Nueng.

334
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,040
See you tomorrow.

335
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:58,840
(How are you getting home this evening, Chat)

336
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:00,360
(Want me to drive you?)

337
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:13,560
I think you should give up on Chat.

338
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:17,640
Even if Jeno weren’t in the picture,

339
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:19,360
he still wouldn’t choose you.

340
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:21,720
I know.

341
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:23,680
But I already have feelings for Chat,

342
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:27,720
and I’m going to give it everything I’ve got.

343
00:24:30,240 --> 00:24:31,560
Aren’t you tired?

344
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:34,200
Why keep trying at something when you know

345
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:35,520
it’s impossible?

346
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,160
You’re not tired yet either, are you?

347
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:48,200
I think

348
00:24:49,120 --> 00:24:50,560
you and I are best off

349
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:53,240
as just friends.

350
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:33,120
Peck, are you okay?

351
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,600
Can’t really put it into words.

352
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:42,920
If you can’t take it, you can go home first.

353
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,800
I’ll cover things here.

354
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:50,720
Why go home?

355
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:53,760
I’d rather work and try to forget about it.

356
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:59,120
Fine. Then let’s get something tasty this evening,

357
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:01,080
I'll treat you to a mookrata. Interested?

358
00:26:01,520 --> 00:26:02,720
You said it.

359
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:03,760
Mmm.

360
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,640
Same place as usual, okay?

361
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:08,040
Yeah, sure.

362
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:11,360
Hmm, he looks clean-cut enough.

363
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:14,600
So what department should we put him in?

364
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:16,080
All done.

365
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:18,160
Chat, June, what are you up to?

366
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:31,000
Hello, everyone. My name is Leo.

367
00:26:31,080 --> 00:26:33,720
I’m the student who’ll be interning with Team B.

368
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:39,320
The appointment was at nine, you show up at five?

369
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:41,880
Look, everyone’s already gone home.

370
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:44,360
Ah, I got held up at a seminar.

371
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:45,960
I’m sorry.

372
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,680
I’m sorry, I’m sorry,

373
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:49,240
I’m sorry, I’m sorry.

374
00:26:49,320 --> 00:26:51,240
From now on, I won't be late again.

375
00:26:52,160 --> 00:26:53,880
Come on, it’s his first time.

376
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:55,560
Then we’ll need to look after him.

377
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:58,840
I’m already busy as hell.

378
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,880
Who has time to babysit?

379
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:02,800
Mmm.

380
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:07,160
Is anyone willing to volunteer to look after him?

381
00:27:08,080 --> 00:27:09,280
Peck will.

382
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:11,640
Hey, why does it have to be me?

383
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:14,800
Aren’t you supposed to keep yourself busy?

384
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:17,160
Looking after a kid won’t kill you, right?

385
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:18,280
See,

386
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,560
the seat is free,

387
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,520
he’d be right next to you.

388
00:27:24,520 --> 00:27:27,960
Then I’ll have Peck look after Leo.

389
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:29,360
What do you think, June?

390
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:30,520
Mmm.

391
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:31,720
And Ja?

392
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:32,720
Sounds good to me.

393
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:35,640
Then I’m counting on you to look after Leo.

394
00:27:37,600 --> 00:27:39,520
I’m in your care,

395
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:40,440
Peck.

396
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:54,280
Did you want to see me for something?

397
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:59,320
I have some documents I'd like you to help me with

398
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:01,520
regarding your project,

399
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:03,160
which I'll be sending to Korea.

400
00:28:04,800 --> 00:28:05,640
Of course.

401
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:37,360
Ms. Mira,

402
00:28:37,440 --> 00:28:39,960
if you ever need me to stick my nose into

403
00:28:40,040 --> 00:28:40,880
oops!

404
00:28:41,280 --> 00:28:42,720
I mean, investigate something for you,

405
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:44,760
just let me know!

406
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:49,560
Seungwoo and Chat have a meeting tonight,

407
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:50,640
just the two of them.

408
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,680
Find out what they're talking about for me.

409
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:57,320
Okay! No problem.

410
00:28:57,400 --> 00:28:59,000
Leave it to me.

411
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,960
You can just tell me first.

412
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:20,480
Instead of saying...

413
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:23,200
Hey, I date for fun. No...

414
00:29:50,520 --> 00:29:51,960
Is this color okay?

415
00:29:54,440 --> 00:29:56,200
This one is fine, but this one isn't.

416
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:57,640
Alright.

417
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:28,680
Is this one okay?

418
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:30,880
No, it's not.

419
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:38,720
I've finished all the work.

420
00:30:38,800 --> 00:30:40,600
Can I go home now?

421
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:48,600
Not yet.

422
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:51,240
What else do you want me to do?

423
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:57,520
Don't you think I deserve a reward

424
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,400
for helping you get through this project?

425
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:03,840
So...

426
00:31:04,560 --> 00:31:06,120
What do you want, then?

427
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:06,960
Thank you.

428
00:32:10,280 --> 00:32:11,240
Then,

429
00:32:12,080 --> 00:32:13,440
I'll head home first.

430
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:25,920
Want me to take you home?

431
00:32:28,520 --> 00:32:29,680
It's late.

432
00:32:33,320 --> 00:32:35,440
It's okay. I can get home by myself.

433
00:32:38,120 --> 00:32:39,080
I know.

434
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:41,320
But I want to take you home.

435
00:32:48,080 --> 00:32:49,120
Chat!

436
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:52,880
I'm here to pick you up and take you home.

437
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:40,560
Chat,

438
00:33:42,120 --> 00:33:44,800
are you close with the new department head?

439
00:33:47,400 --> 00:33:49,720
We've been working together a lot lately.

440
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:52,400
We finish work late, he gives me a ride home.

441
00:33:58,960 --> 00:33:59,960
Next time,

442
00:34:00,440 --> 00:34:02,320
just call me and I'll come pick you up.

443
00:34:03,040 --> 00:34:04,760
I want to help you, too.

444
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:14,520
I'm not going to ask you for another chance.

445
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:17,760
Instead, I'll show you

446
00:34:20,159 --> 00:34:22,199
just how much you mean to me.

447
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:27,679
I love you, Chat.

448
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,560
Hello.

449
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:47,000
Is Mr. Chat there?

450
00:35:47,720 --> 00:35:49,680
Chat is taking a shower right now.

451
00:35:51,520 --> 00:35:53,960
Is there something important you need?

452
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:56,080
I'll pass the message along.

453
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:00,800
It's okay.

454
00:36:01,560 --> 00:36:04,480
Just ask Mr. Chat to call me back when he can.

455
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:27,480
I'll never lose you again.

456
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:47,000
Come with me.

457
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:48,840
Where are you taking me?

458
00:36:58,920 --> 00:37:00,160
Shit!

459
00:37:02,920 --> 00:37:03,920
Oh my gosh!

460
00:37:06,280 --> 00:37:07,440
Oh dear!

461
00:37:07,520 --> 00:37:08,880
The picture of Mr. Chat and Mr. Seungwoo

462
00:37:08,960 --> 00:37:10,760
is circulating all over the company group!

463
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:13,040
It's even in the cafeteria group!

464
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,440
What to do?

465
00:37:18,520 --> 00:37:20,320
Chat is in a big trouble!

466
00:37:21,320 --> 00:37:22,640
Your latte is ready.

467
00:37:23,080 --> 00:37:23,920
Thank you.

468
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,040
Here's your change.

469
00:37:25,120 --> 00:37:26,160
Thank you.

470
00:37:28,160 --> 00:37:31,120
Ms. Mira, I'm really sorry for

471
00:37:31,200 --> 00:37:32,720
the mistakes I've made at work.

472
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:34,760
I should've done better, but...

473
00:37:34,840 --> 00:37:37,960
I've just been really exhausted lately.

474
00:37:38,640 --> 00:37:40,440
This is already excellent.

475
00:37:41,520 --> 00:37:42,520
How so?

476
00:37:46,160 --> 00:37:47,680
Consider it your bonus.

477
00:37:49,680 --> 00:37:50,920
Bonus?

478
00:37:52,120 --> 00:37:54,520
Oh, what can you even do with 400?

479
00:37:54,600 --> 00:37:56,320
Better to just make it 500! A nice, round number.

480
00:37:56,760 --> 00:37:58,880
Dressed so nicely, right?

481
00:38:00,920 --> 00:38:01,960
Shit!

482
00:38:05,480 --> 00:38:06,520
What?

483
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:09,440
Gosh! Even though I was asleep!

484
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:11,320
I didn't even stop my duty!

485
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:12,440
I'm fantastic!

486
00:38:14,080 --> 00:38:15,160
Oh my gosh!

487
00:38:15,240 --> 00:38:16,560
It's brilliant!

488
00:38:16,640 --> 00:38:17,760
Brilliant!

489
00:38:25,520 --> 00:38:26,800
What kind of picture is this?

490
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:28,680
Or could it be the noise from last night?

491
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:18,200
Mr. Seungwoo.

492
00:39:19,040 --> 00:39:21,040
In that case, I’ll go pack my things.

493
00:39:35,080 --> 00:39:36,600
I asked to check the office CCTV footage,

494
00:39:37,040 --> 00:39:38,680
but the cameras are broken.

495
00:39:39,560 --> 00:39:41,120
It'll probably take some time to repair them

496
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:42,440
and recover the footage.

497
00:39:42,520 --> 00:39:44,040
This isn't your fault,

498
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:45,920
so please don't worry.

499
00:39:46,280 --> 00:39:48,080
You've barely been with the company,

500
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:50,120
and you're already causing trouble?

501
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:53,600
You should know that our company

502
00:39:53,680 --> 00:39:55,480
doesn't take kindly to scandals.

503
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:57,480
But I can explain what happened.

504
00:39:57,560 --> 00:39:59,160
There's nothing to explain.

505
00:39:59,640 --> 00:40:01,120
We haven't done anything wrong.

506
00:40:01,200 --> 00:40:02,680
With evidence like that,

507
00:40:02,760 --> 00:40:04,400
you still have the nerve to say it's not wrong?

508
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:05,840
That footage simply shows

509
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:08,360
Mr. Chat and me sitting together while working.

510
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:11,080
The camera angle might make us look close,

511
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:13,480
but nothing inappropriate happened.

512
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:15,240
Isn't that right?

513
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:20,240
Aren't you being protective for someone who's

514
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:22,160
supposed to be his boss?

515
00:40:23,040 --> 00:40:24,120
Not at all.

516
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:27,040
But if being close to an employee

517
00:40:27,120 --> 00:40:28,720
is considered a scandal,

518
00:40:28,800 --> 00:40:31,680
then perhaps I should consult you and Mr. Ford

519
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:34,440
about just how close I'm allowed to be

520
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:38,240
with my employees without causing one.

521
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:55,160
Chat, about that photo...

522
00:40:56,200 --> 00:40:58,600
Mr. Seungwoo and I are just a boss and employee.

523
00:40:58,680 --> 00:41:00,160
There's nothing special between us.

524
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:06,280
Have you gotten back together with Jeno?

525
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:08,280
I can take care of you for

526
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:09,560
the rest of your life now, Chat.

527
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:11,720
Someone has told you

528
00:41:11,800 --> 00:41:13,080
about the rumors circulating

529
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:15,640
among the employees at the company, right?

530
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:17,840
I want you to investigate Seungwoo.

531
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:19,000
I want to know the real reason.

532
00:41:19,080 --> 00:41:20,000
No way someone like him

533
00:41:20,080 --> 00:41:21,880
would abandon everything in Korea

534
00:41:21,960 --> 00:41:23,640
and start over here for no reason.

535
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:26,200
You have only two days left

536
00:41:26,280 --> 00:41:27,920
to prepare your presentation for

537
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:30,280
the multifunctional trend product.

538
00:41:30,360 --> 00:41:32,440
I think we're going to win this round.

539
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:33,960
If we win,

540
00:41:34,040 --> 00:41:35,800
we won't get fired!

541
00:41:35,880 --> 00:41:38,160
I'm treating all of you

542
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:39,720
to mookrata today!

543
00:41:39,800 --> 00:41:40,880
How does that sound?

544
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:42,600
Okay!

545
00:41:42,680 --> 00:41:43,600
What's going on, June?

546
00:41:43,680 --> 00:41:45,680
Huh? What?

547
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:49,560
So they've really gone that far?

548
00:41:49,640 --> 00:41:51,400
I need to sort this out myself.

549
00:41:51,480 --> 00:41:53,000
You want to know what happened, don't you?

550
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:54,320
Me without you, I can manage

551
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:56,600
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

552
00:41:56,680 --> 00:41:59,400
I can still smile, easy and free

553
00:41:59,480 --> 00:42:01,800
Good without you, I’m doing fine

554
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:04,280
Me without you, I can manage

555
00:42:04,360 --> 00:42:06,520
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

556
00:42:06,600 --> 00:42:09,680
I can still smile, easy and free

557
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:12,480
You thought I’d cry cry cry all night

558
00:42:12,560 --> 00:42:14,960
But I’m dancing under neon lights

559
00:42:15,040 --> 00:42:17,480
